Patch 3010: the tick-locked audio's output pays lost game time back faster: absolute feedback gain, a debt of concealed time with a boosted refill, a quick slow-pace entry, and one log line per gap (AUDIO_LOCK_REFILL=0 turns it off).

Symptom (test10 friends' bundles, test11 FORENSICS.md): the sound is short by the game time the match loses (wall time - ticks / 30; a late tick is
never caught up), and 59-77 % of that came out as concealed gaps in every fight, whatever the cushion (50, 90 or 180 ms). There is no bug in the
trigger (concealment starts only under AUDIO_LOCK_LOW_MS, 12 ms; a positive rate is the slower playback that refills); the output repaid too little.
Replaying the per-second fps of rooms 69 and 71 ([RSXFPS]) through the real output in virtual time gives 78 / 146 gaps (4.2 / 7.9 s concealed;
the fights logged 99 / 190 and 4.3 / 6.9 s); with this patch 61 / 115 (3.2 / 5.4 s).

Output only (blocks mixed, read index and notify events are exactly as in 3005; muted re-run blocks are never submitted):
- the feedback's gain is absolute: 1 % per 10 ms off the cushion (was the error divided by the cushion, so a deeper cushion corrected less), capped
  as before at AUDIO_LOCK_DRC/256 both ways;
- the level it reads follows a fall at once (the 0.9 / 0.1 EMA only for a rise), so a stall is answered at the next burst;
- concealed time is owed (at most 500 ms); from the burst that ends a gap, while anything is owed, the refill cap is AUDIO_LOCK_DRC_BOOST/256
  (default 16 = 6.25 %; the feedback and feed-forward total stays capped at 8 %). The feedback's share of each block pays it down (the slow pace
  and the feed-forward cover a slower tick and repay nothing), and it is cleared once the level before a burst is back at the cushion;
- the slow pace (3009) also enters on a short run of slow ticks: two 333 ms buckets in a row under 90 % arrival, neither holding one tick of
  150 ms or more (a single hitch, even 300 ms, never enters). Engaged this way it follows the arrival rate of the last ~1 s and goes down at up to
  0.5 per second, until 3 of 3009's 1 s buckets were made after the entry; the way back is 3009's, and an engagement that never went under 1
  leaves 3009's buckets as they were;
- one "[audio-lock] gap N: tick T, X ms after the last burst began, level before that burst L ms, Y ms concealed, owed D ms" line per gap (the first
  40 of a lock, then every 10th);
- the "[audio-lock]" line keeps every field and their order and appends: "refill: debt max D ms, P ms paid back, quick slow pace N times, boost
  B %, on|off";
- not done here: a pitch-preserving time stretch (WSOLA) for the refill and the slow pace; the playback still changes pitch with its rate;
- with AUDIO_LOCK_REFILL=0 the output is 3009's; the game's lock device is then 200 ms as before (main.cpp), unless AUDIO_LOCK_BUF_MS is set;
- tests: libs/audio/tests/test_audio_lock_race.c part 6, virtual time, 300 ms fake device: steady 30 ticks/s conceals nothing after the start;
  29 fps with a 50-100 ms tick every ~2 s: 21 gaps after 15 s against 76 (3009); runs of 5 / 15 slow ticks: fewer gaps (runs of 80-100 ms ticks
  still mostly conceal: a run loses ~50 ms a tick); single 76 ms and 150-300 ms hitches never engage the slow pace; 20 ticks/s is gap-free once
  settled. Parts 1-4 run with it on (part 4: the feedback still settles at the cushion, not pinned); part 5 runs with it off, so its numbers are
  3009's. audio_lock_measure.c adds a "bundle hitches ~2 s" scenario (50-100 ms every 1-3 s) with the owed time per hitch.

